     mmee is MicroEMACS, a screen editor that keeps the text being
     edited in one or more memory buffers, each shown in its own
     window on the screen.  If _f_i_l_e is given, mmee reads it into a
     buffer named after _f_i_l_e's last component and displays it in
     a window; if _f_i_l_e does not exist, mmee starts an empty buffer
     under that name so the file can be created by saving it
     later.  With no argument, mmee starts with a single empty
     buffer named mmaaiinn.

     Ordinary printable characters typed are inserted at the cur-
     rent position, which lies between two characters rather than
     on one.  Control characters and the two-character sequences
     beginning with EESSCC (the meta prefix) or ^XX (the control-X
     prefix) invoke editing commands, listed below by category.
     ^QQ inserts the following character literally, even if it is
     one of these command characters.

